OL,3,GStrathclyde
OL,4,
OL,5,CThis Evening and Tonight:FStaying dry.
OL,6,FCentral Belt rather cloudy again, with
OL,7,Fbest of the clear spells in Argyll and
OL,8,FAyrshire. Chance of frost and fog
OL,9,Fpatches overnight, chiefly for rural
OL,10,Fparts. Light winds.
OL,11,
OL,12,CWednesday:FSettled, largely dry fare
OL,13,Fwith bright and sunny spells
OL,14,Fincreasing, but early mist and fog may
OL,15,Fbe slow to burn back. Winds light.
OL,16,
OL,17,COutlook for Thursday to Saturday:
OL,18,FPatchy light rain possible in the
OL,19,FCentral Belt and Lanarkshire, while
OL,20,Fthe west stays dry and occasionally
OL,21,Fbright. Moderate easterly breezes.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
